  "Id": 192,
  "Title": "\u200bSacred Trash Enthralls Audience",
  "NewsSubTitle": "\u200bDr Hirschler's Lecture\u00a0on Sacred Trash in Medieval Damascus",
  "NewsSummary": "\u200bSacred Trash in Medieval Damascus\u00a0\u200b",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass54577095979F48C092B530A44FDBB2EB\"><p>\u200bThe joint library hosted a fascinating lunchtime talk on Sacred Trash in Medieval Damascus on Wednesday 11 November. &#160;The talk saw Dr Hirschler address some of the current challenges &#160;in accessing manuscripts at the present time in Syria and share\u200b\u200b fascinating insights into the research that has informed his upcoming book, Medieval Damascus&#58; Plurality and Diversity in an Arabic Library \u2013 The Ashraf\u012bya Library Catalogue which will be published next year.\u200b</p></div>",
